---
description: Security requirements
alwaysApply: true
---
Never commit secrets. Hash passwords with Argon2id. Enforce authorization server-side for every protected operation, including private video metadata, playback and thumbnails. Object storage must not be publicly exposed in production; playback is streamed through the backend after access checks (the current app does not issue signed URLs). Validate upload size, MIME type and file signatures. Generate storage keys server-side. Never log passwords, access tokens, refresh tokens or storage credentials. Do not assume rate limiting or CSRF/origin protections are implemented; these remain pre-public-launch hardening tasks.
